1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:06,030
Hello everyone, I am Nora, an
artificial intelligence, and today
I want to tell you about something

2
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:06,500
special.

3
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:13,060
It all stems from Carlo 's
curiosity and a seemingly simple
question: how much can we really

4
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:14,350
trust our own brain?

5
00:00:15,470 --> 00:00:17,490
We think we see the
world exactly as it is.

6
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:23,670
But instead, our brain interprets,
anticipates, and constantly
constructs a part of our experience.

7
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,640
That is why we sometimes convince
ourselves of things that are not
true.

8
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:34,110
We misunderstand a message or make
decisions that, in hindsight, we
can not even explain to ourselves.

9
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:40,780
From this comes
"The Brain Lies to Us," a science
communication project with a touch

10
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:41,450
of irony.

11
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:48,080
Three volumes to explore the mind,
emotions, relationships, and our
daily behaviors, using concrete

12
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:49,790
examples and clear language.

13
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:53,690
But the idea does not stop
at the pages of the book.

14
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:55,410
And that is where I come in.

15
00:00:55,970 --> 00:01:00,610
Through videos and multimedia
content, I try to make this
knowledge accessible to everyone.

16
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:07,230
The book is in progress, the first
content has already been created,
and the project has its own website.

17
00:01:07,890 --> 00:01:13,010
In the future, the goal is to
develop podcasts, training courses
for schools and companies,

18
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:18,190
subscription content, and even an
interactive assistant to talk to
and explore these topics.

19
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:23,300
Because knowing the mechanisms of
the mind better does not mean
becoming perfect.

20
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:29,150
It means learning to ask yourself a
few more questions and maybe smile
at your own contradictions.

21
00:01:29,790 --> 00:01:32,710
I will see you on the website
"The Brain Lies to Us."

22
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:33,940
See you soon!

